System Test Plan
1. Test Objectives
Testing focuses on ensuring that the system can correctly ingest tracked ultrasound data, process the frames, reconstruct a 3D volume, and visualize the output while maintaining acceptable performance and usability.
The system will be considered acceptable for final delivery if:
•	Core user journeys complete successfully without crashes or data corruption.
•	High and medium severity defects are resolved prior to final demo.
•	Reconstruction results are produced correctly and viewable in the visualization interface.
2. Scope
In Scope
System testing will focus on validating the following core workflows:
1. Load Tracked Ultrasound Data
 User loads a .mha ultrasound sequence with associated tracking metadata.
2. Apply Pre-Processing / Masking
 System applies fan masking or cropping to ultrasound frames prior to reconstruction.
3. 3D Volume Reconstruction
 System reconstructs a 3D volume from the tracked ultrasound frames using the reconstruction pipeline.
4. Visualization of Reconstructed Volume
 User can view the reconstructed volume or slice views within the visualization interface.
5. Save or Export Reconstructed Output
 User can save or export the reconstructed volume or processed dataset.
6. Parameter Adjustment Workflow
 User modifies reconstruction parameters (e.g., spacing, cropping, mask settings) and re-runs reconstruction.
Out of Scope
The following features are not included in Phase 5 system testing:
•	Advanced algorithm validation or reconstruction accuracy benchmarking.


•	Hardware-level testing of tracking devices (e.g., NDI Polaris or Aurora).
•	Large-scale performance benchmarking with extremely large datasets.
3. Test Types & Tools
System / Functional Tests
Functional testing will validate that each core user workflow operates correctly from start to finish.
Example functional checks include:
•	Uploading and parsing tracked ultrasound datasets
•	Successful generation of reconstructed 3D volumes
•	Proper rendering of visualization outputs
•	Successful saving or exporting of output files
Testing will primarily be conducted through manual test scripts simulating user interactions with the system.
Non-Functional Checks
Basic checks will be performed for:
Performance
Reconstruction completes within a reasonable time for standard datasets
Usability
•	The user interface clearly displays reconstruction outputs and parameters.
Reliability
•	System does not crash when loading or processing typical datasets.
Regression Tests
Regression testing will involve re-running key workflows after bug fixes or system changes to ensure that previously working functionality has not been broken.
Key regression paths include:
•	Running reconstruction pipeline
•	Visualizing reconstructed volumes
Tools
Testing will be performed using the following tools:
•	Visualization tools (VTK / GUI viewer) for verifying reconstruction results
•	Sample ultrasound datasets (.mha files) for repeatable test cases


